findings.proposed_fix:
Current line 150:
    return TraceHash(TracesOfFrobenius(C,2^13:B0:=2^12));
Replacement (self-contained; good primes by point counting, bad window primes via the Euler factor exactly as the genus 2 fast path already does):
    return TraceHash(func<p|IsDivisibleBy(D,p) select -Coefficient(euler(C,p),1) else p+1-#ChangeRing(C,GF(p))>) where D := Integers()!Discriminant(C);
Note: this requires moving the SlowTraceHash intrinsic below the definition of euler (line 156), or inlining 'Genus(C) eq 2 and Conductor(C,p) eq 0 select Genus2AlmostGoodEulerFactor(C,p) else EulerFactor(C,p)'. Alternatively, ship the missing TracesOfFrobenius(C::CrvHyp,B::RngIntElt:B0:=0) intrinsic this line expects. (Also note #ChangeRing(C,GF(p)) requires a p-integral model; window primes are > 8191-free in typical minimal models, and IsDivisibleBy(D,p) guards non-smooth reductions.)

